+
+---
+
+Dear EIS hiring team,
+
+I am applying for the **z/OS Systems Administrator (Information Systems Specialist 8)** role. The position calls for **advanced IBM Z / z/OS** expertise—capacity planning, subsystem configuration, vendor evaluation, and high-severity troubleshooting for **shared statewide services**. That is **not** the primary focus of my recent hands-on work, which has centered on **distributed applications, SQL-heavy platforms, and enterprise integrations**.
+
+What I offer is a **strong operations mindset**: disciplined change management, written operational clarity, cross-agency coordination, and calm execution when services are degraded. If EIS considers candidates who can grow into deeper **systems programming** depth with structured training, I am **explicitly willing to invest in z/OS skills** aligned with your standards. If the req requires Day-1 expert systems programming, I understand I may not be the right fit—and I still appreciate the mission this role protects.
+
+I hold a **BS in Computer Information Systems**, am a **U.S. veteran**, and am motivated by **statewide infrastructure** that must remain dependable as security and complexity increase.
+
+Thank you for reviewing my materials.
+
+Best regards,  
+*[Your name]*
