+# Cover letter — Oregon OWRD Senior Systems & Network Engineer (job rotation), REQ-199237
+
+**Posting:** [Senior Systems & Network Engineer — Limited Duration / Job Rotation](https://oregon.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/SOR_External_Career_Site/job/Salem--OWRD--North-Mall-Office-Building/Senior-Systems---Network-Engineer--Information-Systems-Specialist-7--Limited-Duration-and-or-Job-Rotation_REQ-199237?q=it) — Water Resources Department  
+**JD:** [`653-myworkdayjobs-senior-systems-network-engineer-info-199237-2026-05-07.md`](653-myworkdayjobs-senior-systems-network-engineer-info-199237-2026-05-07.md)
+
+---
+
+Dear OWRD hiring team,
+
+**Eligibility note (please edit to your situation):** This posting states applicants must be **current State of Oregon employees in permanent positions** with **supervisor approval** attached to the application for the **job rotation** path. *[Replace this sentence with: e.g., “I am a permanent classified/state employee and have attached supervisor approval.” or “I am applying only if an external pathway exists—please advise.”]*
+
+I am interested in the **Senior Systems & Network Engineer** rotation supporting OWRD’s **infrastructure unit**: secure networks, systems administration, **cybersecurity and compliance**, troubleshooting, **backup/DR**, and **COOP**-adjacent resilience—work that keeps a small agency IT team effective as complexity grows.
+
+My background emphasizes **enterprise delivery and operational rigor** (cross-functional programs, documentation, incident discipline, and server-side migrations). I would welcome a conversation about how OWRD splits responsibilities with **Enterprise Information Services**, what **hybrid** cadence works for this team, and where you most need **senior consultation** vs. hands-on engineering in the near term.
+
+I hold a **BS in Computer Information Systems**, am a **U.S. veteran**, and care about **sustainable water stewardship** and OWRD’s service values.
+
+Thank you for your consideration.
+
+Best regards,  
+*[Your name]*
