+
+---
+
+Dear ODOT hiring team,
+
+I am applying for **Senior Database Administrator (Information Systems Specialist 8), REQ-200017** on the Enterprise Technology team.
+
+Your posting emphasizes **data modeling**, **secure exchange** (batch and near-real-time), **governance**, **performance tuning**, and partnership on **analytics and AI/ML infrastructure**. That is close to how I have worked on **production data paths** where store, order, and customer systems must stay correct under load: schema design, SQL troubleshooting, integration contracts, and coordination with application teams when failures affect statewide operations.
+
+I have deep hands-on experience with **Microsoft SQL Server** and **PostgreSQL**, stored procedures, and refactoring data access for performance and maintainability. I have designed and operated **batch and file-based pipelines** (SFTP, scheduled jobs, upstream validation) and supported **metadata and operational clarity** so on-call engineers can recover quickly. I am **transparent that dedicated IBM DB2 and Oracle DBA ownership has not been the center of my recent role**; I am motivated to grow those platforms where ODOT values transferable modeling, integration, and governance strength alongside formal database administration depth.
+
+I hold a **BS in Computer Information Systems**, am a **U.S. veteran**, and welcome **hybrid Salem-area** work. I would value discussing how your team balances **on-prem vs. cloud**, DR expectations, and pairing models for engineers expanding across DB2, SQL Server, and Oracle.
+
+Thank you for your consideration.
+
+Best regards,  
+Terry J. Mork
