+**Posting:** [Information Architect](https://oregon.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/SOR_External_Career_Site/job/Salem--DAS--Print-Plant/Information-Architect--Information-Systems-Spec6-_REQ-199857) — Enterprise Information Services, Strategy and Design  
+**JD:** [`759-myworkdayjobs-information-architect-information-sy-199857-2026-05-26.md`](../jds/759-myworkdayjobs-information-architect-information-sy-199857-2026-05-26.md)
+
+---
+
+Dear EIS hiring team,
+
+I am applying for **Information Architect (Information Systems Specialist 6), REQ-199857** in **Strategy and Design**.
+
+The role’s focus—aligning **business capabilities**, **information domains**, and **technology**; supporting **enterprise standards**; mapping relationships among processes, applications, and data; and producing durable **documentation**—matches how I have operated during large **platform migrations** and **integration programs** in complex enterprise settings.
+
+I am strongest where architecture meets **execution discipline**: clarifying non-functional requirements (security, operability, ownership), translating agency pain points into **integration patterns** teams can repeat, and preserving **traceability** so audits and future modernization do not start from zero. I have partnered with product, operations, and engineering leads who do not share the same technical vocabulary and have mentored engineers through **API contracts**, **data boundaries**, and release coordination.
+
+I hold a **BS in Computer Information Systems**, am a **U.S. veteran**, and welcome **hybrid** collaboration in the Salem area. I would value discussing how EIS measures “fit for purpose” across proposed agency solutions and how this role interfaces with **Data Governance and Transparency** initiatives.
+
+Thank you for considering my application.
+
+Best regards,  
+Terry J. Mork
