+# Cover letter — Oregon OWRD Senior GIS Coordinator & Application Developer (ISS 6), REQ-199924
+
+**Posting:** [Senior ArcGIS Coordinator & Application Developer](https://oregon.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/SOR_External_Career_Site/job/Salem--OWRD--North-Mall-Office-Building/Senior-ArcGIS-Coordinator---Application-Developer_REQ-199924) — Oregon Water Resources Department  
+**JD:** [`760-myworkdayjobs-senior-gis-coordinator-application-d-199924-2026-05-26.md`](../jds/760-myworkdayjobs-senior-gis-coordinator-application-d-199924-2026-05-26.md)
+
+---
+
+Dear OWRD hiring team,
+
+I am applying for **Senior GIS Coordinator & Application Developer (Information Systems Specialist 6), REQ-199924**.
+
+The posting describes an interdisciplinary lead who can **guide a capable technical team**, deliver **ArcGIS platform solutions**, and bring strong **application development** skills—**Python**, **relational databases**, **data integrity**, and **Microsoft-stack** administration concerns. That combination aligns with my background in **full-stack delivery**, **SQL-heavy integrations**, and **technical leadership** (about five engineers) on programs where bad data or broken releases had real operational impact.
+
+I have built and maintained **production web applications**, internal tools, and integration layers; mentored engineers on **SQL and JavaScript**; and coordinated releases with operations partners. I am **direct that ArcGIS-specific development is not my primary specialty today**; I am motivated to ramp on **ESRI patterns** while contributing immediately on **scripting, data quality, API/integration design**, team coordination, and disciplined documentation—skills your team needs alongside geospatial depth.
+
+OWRD’s mission—**sustainable water supply** and **healthy streamflows and watersheds**—is meaningful public work. I hold a **BS in Computer Information Systems**, am a **U.S. veteran**, and am interested in the **hybrid Salem** arrangement described.
+
+Thank you for your consideration.
+
+Best regards,  
+Terry J. Mork
