+
+---
+
+Dear DAS hiring team,
+
+I am applying for **Senior Applications Developer (Information Systems Specialist 8), REQ-199700** supporting statewide **financial** systems under the Office of the State Controller.
+
+I understand this team sustains **IBM mainframe applications** using **COBOL, CICS, JCL**, and related tooling—technologies that are not the center of my most recent delivery work, which has focused on **large-scale web platforms, SQL-heavy integrations, and enterprise SaaS**.
+
+What I bring is **discipline in production systems**: breaking down complex inherited behavior, coordinating releases with operations, mentoring peers, and documenting systems so fiscal and reporting workflows stay auditable and stable. I am motivated by **public-service technology** where mistakes show up as delayed payments, broken reports, or frustrated agencies—and I am **prepared to invest in formal skill-building** in the COBOL/CICS stack if DAS selects candidates with adjacent strength who can ramp with training support.
+
+I hold a **BS in Computer Information Systems**, am a **U.S. veteran**, and am interested in **hybrid Salem-area** work as described. I would welcome a conversation about how your team balances **new development vs. maintenance**, modernization roadmaps, and pairing models for engineers expanding into the mainframe environment.
+
+Thank you for considering my application.
+
+Best regards,  
+Terry J. Mork
