+# Cover letter — Oregon DAS z/OS Systems Administrator (ISS 8), REQ-196649
+
+**Posting:** [z/OS Systems Administrator](https://oregon.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/SOR_External_Career_Site/job/Salem--DAS--State-Data-Center/z-OS-Systems-Administrator--Information-Systems-Specialist-8-_REQ-196649) — Enterprise Information Services, Data Center Services  
+**JD:** [`762-myworkdayjobs-z-os-systems-administrator-informati-196649-2026-05-26.md`](../jds/762-myworkdayjobs-z-os-systems-administrator-informati-196649-2026-05-26.md)
+
+---
+
+Dear EIS hiring team,
+
+I am applying for **z/OS Systems Administrator (Information Systems Specialist 8), REQ-196649**.
+
+The position calls for **advanced IBM Z / z/OS** expertise—capacity planning, subsystem configuration, vendor evaluation, and high-severity troubleshooting for **shared statewide services**. That is **not** the primary focus of my recent hands-on work, which has centered on **distributed applications, SQL-heavy platforms, and enterprise integrations**.
+
+What I offer is a **strong operations mindset**: disciplined change management, written operational clarity, cross-agency coordination, and calm execution when services are degraded. If EIS considers candidates who can grow into deeper **systems programming** depth with structured training, I am **explicitly willing to invest in z/OS skills** aligned with your standards. If the req requires Day-1 expert systems programming, I understand I may not be the right fit—and I still appreciate the mission this role protects.
+
+I hold a **BS in Computer Information Systems**, am a **U.S. veteran**, and am motivated by **statewide infrastructure** that must remain dependable as security and complexity increase.
+
+Thank you for reviewing my materials.
+
+Best regards,  
+Terry J. Mork
