+# Cover letter — Costco Travel, Software Engineer (Booking)
+
+**Posting:** [Software Engineer - Booking - Costco Travel](https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=COSTCO&cws=41&rid=10424)  
+**Location:** Issaquah (Seattle), WA  
+**Order Number:** 10424
+
+---
+
+Dear Costco Travel IT hiring team,
+
+I am applying for the **Software Engineer (Booking)** role on Costco Travel IT. The work you describe, member-facing booking flows, account management, SSO, checkout, payment gateway integrations, and configuration services for travel products, is the same class of problems I have owned in large-scale retail: high-traffic customer paths where correctness, performance, and calm production response matter.
+
+I am a senior full-stack engineer with **10+ years** building client-server and web applications end to end. My recent delivery has been strongest in **JavaScript/TypeScript, Node.js, React, REST APIs, SQL, and enterprise integrations**, including **checkout-adjacent flows, authentication (JWT/session, OAuth, Okta-class patterns), and payment-related integrations** at Bath & Body Works and Saks OFF 5TH. I have also shipped production **C# / ASP.NET** work earlier in my career and am comfortable ramping quickly in **Java, JSP, and MVC-style service design** when the domain and team practices are clear. I treat object-oriented design, unit testing, and API contracts as non-negotiable, which maps directly to your Agile booking stack and microservice boundaries.
+
+What draws me to Costco Travel IT specifically is the combination of **retail scale** and **mission-critical member experience**. I have led and contributed to major platform change efforts (headless commerce migration, email platform integration, multi-region rollout) while using **Splunk** and modern monitoring practices to debug production bottlenecks. I work well in scrum teams, estimate my own work honestly, and partner with QA and product without needing heavy supervision. I am motivated by stable, respectful engineering culture and by systems that serve millions of members reliably.
+
+I would welcome the opportunity to help the Booking team deliver secure, fast, maintainable solutions across your Java/JSP and REST service landscape. Thank you for considering my application.
+
+Sincerely,  
+Terry J. Mork  
+tmork.dev@gmail.com  
+https://www.linkedin.com/in/terryjmork/
+
+---
+
+_Paste the letter body (from "Dear Costco Travel IT…" through signature) into the Taleo **Cover Letter** field, or upload as PDF alongside your resume._
