+<div class="page">
+  <h1>Cover letter — Oregon DLCD Application Developer (ISS6), REQ-201322</h1>
+  <div class="gradient"></div>
+  <div class="meta-line"><strong>Posting:</strong> [Application Developer (ISS6)](<a href="https://oregon.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/SOR_External_Career_Site/job/Salem-%7C-DLCD/Application-Developer--ISS6-_REQ-201322)">https://oregon.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/SOR_External_Career_Site/job/Salem-%7C-DLCD/Application-Developer--ISS6-_REQ-201322)</a> — Land Conservation and Development Department, Data Management and Production Services (DMAPS)</div>
+  <div style="height:10px"></div>
+  <p>Dear DLCD hiring team,</p>
+<p>I am writing to express strong interest in the <strong>Application Developer (Information Systems Specialist 6)</strong> role in <strong>DMAPS</strong>. The posting’s mix of <strong>modern web development (Python, JavaScript, HTML/CSS)</strong>, <strong>SQL Server and PostgreSQL</strong>, <strong>legacy .NET modernization</strong>, <strong>ArcGIS-backed spatial workflows</strong>, and <strong>data discoverability</strong> aligns closely with how I have delivered production systems: end-to-end ownership from UI through databases, ticket-driven support, and documentation that keeps agency codebases maintainable over time.</p>
+<p>In enterprise environments I have <strong>built and operated full-stack applications</strong>, <strong>designed SQL schemas and stored procedures</strong>, and <strong>owned scheduled jobs and integrations</strong> where downtime directly affected staff and customers. At National Data Systems I ramped on <strong>C#/ASP.NET</strong> in production, refactored onboarding into parameter-driven business rules with <strong>JavaScript and SQL Server</strong>, and mentored peers until they could work independently. More recently, as technical lead at Bath &amp; Body Works, I coordinated <strong>60+ scheduled jobs</strong>, production data paths, API standards, and cross-team delivery—experience that maps well to supporting internal applications, automated processes, and collaboration with a <strong>Data Engineer</strong> on accessible, well-governed agency data.</p>
+<p>I am especially drawn to DLCD’s mission: equitable land-use planning supported by reliable tools and clear metadata. I bring a <strong>BS in Computer Information Systems</strong>, <strong>ArcGIS familiarity</strong> alongside broader integration work, comfort on <strong>Linux and Windows</strong> server environments, and a track record of <strong>clear written documentation and cross-team coordination</strong>. I am an <strong>Oregon resident</strong>, a <strong>U.S. veteran</strong>, and welcome the <strong>hybrid Salem-area</strong> arrangement described in the announcement.</p>
+<p>I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how DMAPS prioritizes <strong>Django/Python modernization</strong>, <strong>ArcGIS Enterprise/Online</strong> enhancements, and migration planning for legacy .NET applications—and how I can help reduce risk while improving data access for DLCD staff and partners.</p>
+<p>Thank you for your consideration.</p>
+<p>Best regards,   Terry J. Mork</p>
+</div>
+</body>
