+# Cover letter — Oregon DLCD Application Developer (ISS6), REQ-201322
+
+**Posting:** [Application Developer (ISS6)](https://oregon.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/SOR_External_Career_Site/job/Salem-%7C-DLCD/Application-Developer--ISS6-_REQ-201322) — Land Conservation and Development Department, Data Management and Production Services (DMAPS)
+
+---
+
+Dear DLCD hiring team,
+
+I am writing to express strong interest in the **Application Developer (Information Systems Specialist 6)** role in **DMAPS**. The posting’s mix of **modern web development (Python, JavaScript, HTML/CSS)**, **SQL Server and PostgreSQL**, **legacy .NET modernization**, **ArcGIS-backed spatial workflows**, and **data discoverability** aligns closely with how I have delivered production systems: end-to-end ownership from UI through databases, ticket-driven support, and documentation that keeps agency codebases maintainable over time.
+
+In enterprise environments I have **built and operated full-stack applications**, **designed SQL schemas and stored procedures**, and **owned scheduled jobs and integrations** where downtime directly affected staff and customers. At National Data Systems I ramped on **C#/ASP.NET** in production, refactored onboarding into parameter-driven business rules with **JavaScript and SQL Server**, and mentored peers until they could work independently. More recently, as technical lead at Bath & Body Works, I coordinated **60+ scheduled jobs**, production data paths, API standards, and cross-team delivery—experience that maps well to supporting internal applications, automated processes, and collaboration with a **Data Engineer** on accessible, well-governed agency data.
+
+I am especially drawn to DLCD’s mission: equitable land-use planning supported by reliable tools and clear metadata. I bring a **BS in Computer Information Systems**, **ArcGIS familiarity** alongside broader integration work, comfort on **Linux and Windows** server environments, and a track record of **clear written documentation and cross-team coordination**. I am an **Oregon resident**, a **U.S. veteran**, and welcome the **hybrid Salem-area** arrangement described in the announcement.
+
+I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how DMAPS prioritizes **Django/Python modernization**, **ArcGIS Enterprise/Online** enhancements, and migration planning for legacy .NET applications—and how I can help reduce risk while improving data access for DLCD staff and partners.
+
+Thank you for your consideration.
+
+Best regards,  
+Terry J. Mork
+
