+
+At Bath & Body Works I worked across **headless commerce**, **SAP**, **Salesforce Marketing Cloud**, and analytics pipelines, with a steady focus on **contracts, retries, and operational correctness** on paths that touch checkout, authentication, and fraud-adjacent flows. I am comfortable in **Python** and **JavaScript/Node**, have delivered with **Golang** where the team standardized on it, and I lean on **Postgres** and **SQL Server** when the schema is part of the product. Cloud-wise I have shipped on **AWS** and **Azure** and treat **CI/CD**, testing, and observability as part of the feature, not an afterthought. I have also **mentored** engineers and led cross-functional programs—for example directing the nationwide **BOPIS** rollout across **114** stores—so I understand the balance between deep technical work and keeping stakeholders aligned when timelines slip.
+
+Quanata’s mission—**context-based insurance** backed by serious infrastructure—appeals to me because it is the same class of problem I know from retail at scale: regulated-feeling data, many moving parts, and zero tolerance for silent failure. I will be direct: I have not spent a career inside **underwriting** systems, but I ramp quickly when paired with strong domain owners, and I already care about the **security and reliability** habits your posting emphasizes.
+
